course: dictionary
lesson: 6208
title: Words from places and history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a place, a group of people, or a time long ago. Mississippian is one of these words. Look for clues around it: a place name, a capital letter, or words like «built» and «million years» tell you what kind of thing the word is about.
explain: Mississippian can be a noun, naming a person from the US state of Mississippi, as in «a Mississippian». It can also be an adjective, describing something, as in «Mississippian people». Check the job the word does in the sentence: is it naming someone, or describing something?
explain: The same word also names a time in Earth's history. Science books use it this way, so the clues are words like «million years» and rock. When you meet a word like this, read the sentence around it and ask what kind of thing it describes.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Mississippian» can be a noun (a Mississippian is a person from the US state of Mississippi) or an adjective (Mississippian people).
fact: The Mississippian culture was a Native American civilisation that built great earth mounds along the Mississippi valley, from about 800 to 1600.
fact: Mississippian is also a period of Earth's history, about 359 to 323 million years ago, used in the USA.
fact: «Estimates» are careful guesses, not exact counts, so the numbers for Cahokia are estimates.
exercise: «Cahokia was built by Mississippian people.» What does Mississippian describe here? | A kind of rock | *The people who built the city | A type of coal | A month of the year
exercise: A Mississippian is a person from which place? | *The US state of Mississippi | Ireland | Australia | Scotland
exercise: Which word in «The Mississippian culture built great earth mounds» is an adjective? | *Mississippian | built | mounds | culture
test: Mississippian is a period of Earth's history about 359 to 323 million years ago. Which clue tells you it is about a very long time ago? | The name St Louis | The capital letter at the start | *Million years | The word culture
test: The Mississippian culture lasted from about 800 to 1600. About how many years did it last? | 50 years | *About 800 years | 2,000 years | 10 years
exam: What does «estimates» mean in «the numbers are estimates»? | *Careful guesses, not exact counts | Exact counts that are always right | Stories from long ago | Maps of the city
